    "reviewed_claims": [
      {
        "topic": "Exact variants, bindings, and tier differences",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "Canonical config and extension evidence agree: P1 powersword trait covers Mk III and Mk VI at 5/10/15/20%; P3 covers Branx Mk VI at 4/6/8/10%. All three bindings and both actual trait IDs are reflected in the eight formal pages."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Held and special-active conditions",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "The base class-buff wrapper gates conditional keywords and heavy-damage stat on both the applicable item being wielded and that item slot special_active. Formal prose also separates cache update from native special state."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Actual HitMass target branch and remaining stops",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "The quarter-mass effect applies only to the eligible living enemy breed-character branch, excluding players, props, and living props. Armor-abort is bypassed while independent max-hit-mass and breed-abort limits remain; target armor still participates in damage calculation."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Heavy-damage consumer and active profiles",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "melee_heavy_damage enters the damage-stat pool only for melee attacks whose actual damage profile strength is heavy. P1 and P3 own tiers replace the base .05 fallback. P1 push-follow profiles on both marks and the P3 push-follow are light strength, so they do not receive the heavy-damage increment."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Native special timing, first effect, and switching",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "P1 has a three-second single-attack window that can be reactivated while active and is closed by switching away. P3 has four seconds and up to six charges; unused charge can remain after switching while held/special-active eligibility is off. Blessing adds no independent trigger stack, cooldown, or timer."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Formula and isolated examples",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "P1 IV 100×(1+.20)=120 and P3 IV 100×(1+.10)=110 under explicitly neutral other damage modifiers and downstream multipliers; formal prose keeps these stat-pool deltas distinct from guaranteed final health damage."
      },
      {
        "topic": "RAW comparison and errata scope",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "The comparison records English Increased Cleave and the ambiguous Traditional Chinese “提高順劈攻擊傷害”. It classifies the missing mechanics as document not covered and does not claim a definite contradiction that all light attacks gain direct damage."
      },
      {
        "topic": "Eight-page links, icon, and global associations",
        "result": "pass",
        "detail": "All eight formal entry documents, all other scoped association/index/glossary files, and the preflight inventory match the frozen scope hashes. The candidate preflight reports eight pages, valid local paths, and no issues; the exact weapon icon is consistently referenced."
